#: markdown/inputs.md:1
msgid "Input files"
msgstr "入力ファイル"

#: markdown/inputs.md:3
msgid ""
"All files and data required to perform this tutorial are on the [GitHub "
"repository](https://github.com/blake-armstrong/binding-tutorial-PLUMED). "
"They can either be accessed by cloning the repository to your machine;"
msgstr ""
"全ファイルは [GitHub](https://github.com/blake-armstrong/binding-tutorial-PLUMED) "
"にあり、Clone するか、"

#: markdown/inputs.md:9
msgid ""
"or by following the download instructions in the `README.md` page on the "
"repository to download the basic ZIP file."
msgstr "リポジトリの `README.md` の手順で基本 ZIP を取得できます。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:11
msgid ""
"Once downloaded, the input files required to run a simulation with OpenMM "
"and PLUMED are provided in the `simulation_files` directory. Included in the"
" `scripts` directory are bash scripts that will automate setting up the "
"multiple-walker simulation files and will analyse the output for you. These "
"scripts are not strictly necessary to perform this tutorial, as the actions "
"they perform can be carried out manually by the user. All the data has "
"already been produced and analysed, and is presented in the 'data' "
"directory. We will discuss how that data was produced and analysed so you "
"can do it all yourself."
msgstr ""
"OpenMM・PLUMED の入力は `simulation_files` にあります。`scripts` の Bash は Multiple "
"Walker の設定と出力解析を自動化しますが、手動でもできるため必須ではありません。計算・解析済みデータは data "
"にあります。生成・解析の方法を、自分でも行えるよう説明します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:13
msgid "OpennMM & PLUMED Installation"
msgstr "OpenMM と PLUMED のインストール"

#: markdown/inputs.md:15
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is get a working installation of OpenMM and "
"openmmplumed. [Comprehensive installation instructions for "
"OpenMM](http://docs.openmm.org/latest/userguide/application/01_getting_started.html)."
" We recommend using `conda`, as it is the most straight forward way to "
"install the software without needing to worry about dependencies. See "
"[instructions for installing "
"conda](https://conda.io/projects/conda/en/latest/user-"
"guide/install/index.html). After testing the installation with:"
msgstr ""
"まず OpenMM と openmmplumed を動かせるようにします。[OpenMM "
"の詳細手順](http://docs.openmm.org/latest/userguide/application/01_getting_started.html)"
" を参照してください。依存を扱いやすい `conda` "
"を推奨します（[導入手順](https://conda.io/projects/conda/en/latest/user-"
"guide/install/index.html)）。次で確認します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:21
msgid ""
"All platforms available to you will be shown. In this tutorial we use the "
"CPU platform, and the input files provided set up a simulation to use the "
"CPU platform, which every user should have available by default. The "
"[instructions to install the OpenMM PLUMED "
"plugin](https://github.com/openmm/openmm-plumed) are also very simple when "
"using conda. This will also install the command line plumed tool which will "
"be used for analysis later on."
msgstr ""
"利用可能な Platform が表示されます。ここでは、通常誰でも使える CPU を入力で指定しています。conda なら [OpenMM PLUMED"
" Plugin](https://github.com/openmm/openmm-plumed) も簡単に入れられ、後の解析用 PLUMED "
"コマンドも入ります。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:23
msgid "Running a simulation"
msgstr "シミュレーションの実行"

#: markdown/inputs.md:25
msgid "Running the bash script `setup_walkers.sh`"
msgstr "`setup_walkers.sh` を実行すると、"

#: markdown/inputs.md:31
msgid "or"
msgstr "または"

#: markdown/inputs.md:37
msgid ""
"will create a set of directory trees within the `data` directory labelled "
"with cylinder radii ranging from 0.0 nm to 0.5 nm. `NUMWALKERS` is an "
"integer for the number of walkers desired with the default being 4 (NB this "
"can be changed but must be greater than 1 for multiple walker metadynamics)."
" These directories are where the multiple walker simulations will be run for"
" systems with various radii for the flat-bottom cylindrical restraining "
"potential. This setup script has been included so that the user can play "
"around with different numbers of walkers in an easy way, if they so desire. "
"By default, it will create directories and setups for four walkers. The "
"details on how to run a single walker are discussed further later."
msgstr ""
"`data` に半径0.0〜0.5 nm のディレクトリを作ります。`NUMWALKERS` は Walker "
"数の整数で、既定は4です。Multiple Walker では1超にします。各半径の Flat-bottom 円柱の実行先です。Walker "
"数を容易に変えて試せます。Single Walker は後述します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:39
msgid "If we navigate to the directory for a radius of 0.0 nm,"
msgstr "半径0.0 nm のディレクトリに移ると、"

#: markdown/inputs.md:45
msgid ""
"here we will find a `run.sh` script here that will handle submitting the "
"run.py job for each walker. The `run.py` file (which is located in the "
"`simulation_files` directory) will allow us to run our simulation using "
"OpenMM through its Python API. The `plumed.inp` file which contains the "
"PLUMED specifics. There is an 'analysis.sh' script here as well, which will "
"handle the analysis of our simulation output, which is discussed "
"[here](analysis.md)."
msgstr ""
"各 Walker の run.py を投入する `run.sh` があります。`simulation_files` の `run.py` は "
"OpenMM Python API で実行します。`plumed.inp` は PLUMED の設定です。出力解析用 analysis.sh "
"もあり、[こちら](analysis.md) で説明します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:47
msgid ""
"There is [extensive documentation for using the OpenMM Python "
"API](http://docs.openmm.org/latest/userguide/application/02_running_sims.html)"
" which we direct you to if you cannot understand some component of the "
"`run.py` file while we briefly discuss it here."
msgstr ""
"ここで `run.py` を簡単に説明します。不明な部分は [OpenMM Python API "
"の詳細](http://docs.openmm.org/latest/userguide/application/02_running_sims.html)"
" を参照してください。"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: markdown/inputs.md:49
msgid "run.py"
msgstr "run.py"

#: markdown/inputs.md:58
msgid ""
"These lines give us access to the OpenMM code, and the OpenMM PLUMED plugin "
"that can parse a PLUMED input file, interpret it, and provide the "
"instructions to OpenMM."
msgstr "これらの行で OpenMM と、PLUMED 入力を解釈して OpenMM に指示を渡す Plugin を使えるようにします。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:74
msgid ""
"Simulation parameter definitions that will be used further in the file. When"
" providing a unit with a dimension, we make use of the OpenMM unit object. "
"By default, each walker will run for 2 ns which should take 5 - 10 minutes "
"to complete. This should be enough to produce a PMF that is sufficiently "
"converged to analyse for our purposes due to the simplicity of the model "
"system."
msgstr ""
"後で使うパラメータを定義します。次元のある量には OpenMM Unit Object を使います。既定で各 Walker は2 "
"ns、約5〜10分です。単純な系なので目的に十分収束した PMF が得られるはずです。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:93 markdown/inputs.md:165
msgid ""
"The details of this section are better explained in the [OpenMM "
"docs](http://docs.openmm.org/latest/userguide/application/02_running_sims.html)."
msgstr ""
"この部分の詳細は "
"[OpenMM](http://docs.openmm.org/latest/userguide/application/02_running_sims.html)"
" を参照してください。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:102
msgid ""
"This section is needed to prevent the thermal energy from being removed from"
" the system as we have only one particle. It is not important to understand,"
" as it would not generally be necessary for a real simulation."
msgstr "1粒子だけなので熱エネルギーが除去されるのを防ぐ部分です。通常の実系には不要なので、理解は必須ではありません。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:109
msgid ""
"This is where a PLUMED input script is read and our forces will be created "
"and added to the system."
msgstr "PLUMED 入力を読み、力を生成して系に加えます。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:167
msgid "plumed.inp"
msgstr "plumed.inp"

#: markdown/inputs.md:169
msgid ""
"Here we will discuss all of the sections of the PLUMED input file "
"(plumed.inp)."
msgstr "PLUMED 入力 plumed.inp の全部分を説明します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:175
msgid ""
"Required for multiple walkers. Ensures each walker reads HILLS from all "
"walkers when initialised."
msgstr "Multiple Walkers に必要で、初期化時に全 Walker の HILLS を読むようにします。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:180
msgid ""
"Simulation units. Same as OpenMM units for consistency. Not a necessity."
msgstr "単位を OpenMM に合わせます。必須ではありません。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:186
msgid ""
"Here we define our z-distance that we will use for the collective variable. "
"We define a fixed point at the middle of our cubic simulation box (50 Å in "
"each direction) and calculate the distance between the fixed point and our "
"one particle, and save it to the `d1` variable."
msgstr "CV の z 距離を定義します。各方向50 Å の立方体 Box の中心に固定点を置き、1粒子との距離を `d1` に保存します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:203
msgid ""
"Here we use the x and y components of the d1 variable to create `rd`, the "
"flat-bottomed cylindrical restraining potential. We then tell PLUMED to "
"actually use the potential to apply forces throughout the simulation, and "
"not just record its value."
msgstr ""
"d1 の x・y 成分から Flat-bottom 円柱 Potential `rd` を作り、値の記録だけでなく実際に力を加えるよう指定します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:214
msgid ""
"Here we define upper and lower harmonic walls in the z-dimension. The lower "
"wall emulates the repulsion of a surface, and starts acting on the particle "
"at -0.125 nm in the z direction. The upper wall prevents the binding atom "
"from going too far from the `surface` in the z-direction, and starts acting "
"at 1.5 nm."
msgstr ""
"z に上下の Harmonic Wall を定義します。下は表面の反発を模し、-0.125 nm から働きます。上は `surface` "
"から離れすぎないよう1.5 nm から働きます。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:252
msgid ""
"The following is used to create an arbitrary potential energy surface that "
"mimics the binding profile of an atom normal to a surface. There will be a "
"minimum at [2.5, 2.5, 2.5] nm to represent a stable surface site and a "
"maximum at [2.5, 2.5, 2.8] nm to represent a barrier for leaving the "
"surface."
msgstr ""
"表面法線方向の結合を模す Potential Energy Surface を作ります。[2.5, 2.5, 2.5] nm の極小が安定な表面 "
"Site、[2.5, 2.5, 2.8] nm の極大が解離 Barrier です。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:291
msgid ""
"This will output a collective variable file to monitor that everything in "
"the simulation is proceeding as expected."
msgstr "CV を出力して、意図した挙動か監視します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:296
msgid ""
"This will flush the output every 1000 steps, allowing us to monitor that "
"everything within PLUMED is working as it should while the simulation is "
"running."
msgstr "1000 Step ごとに出力を Flush し、実行中も PLUMED の動作を確認できます。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:320
msgid ""
"This tells PLUMED to run multiple walker metadynamics with a collective "
"variable defined as the z-component of the `d1` distance. WALKERS_ID and "
"WALKERS_N are set to placeholder names which will get replaced when "
"submitting the job through the `run.sh` script. While the multiple walkers "
"run, the HILLS files will be written to and read from the 'BIAS' directory. "
"If you wish to run a single walker simulation, the `RESTART` keyword should "
"be removed, alongside the last four lines inside the `METAD` section. The "
"`HILLS` file will then be written inside the current directory instead of a "
"dedicated `BIAS` directory. The analysis scripts will then need to be "
"modified accordingly."
msgstr ""
"`d1` の z 成分を CV とする Multiple Walker Metadynamics を指定します。WALKERS_ID、WALKERS_N"
" の仮名は `run.sh` が置換します。実行中 HILLS は BIAS で読み書きします。Single Walker では `RESTART` と"
" `METAD` の最後の4行を除きます。`HILLS` は `BIAS` ではなく現ディレクトリに出るので、解析スクリプトも調整します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:322
msgid "run.sh"
msgstr "run.sh"

#: markdown/inputs.md:324
msgid ""
"The `run.sh` file will handle submitting all of the walkers for a given "
"simulation."
msgstr "`run.sh` は全 Walker を投入します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:329
msgid ""
"The `OPENMM_CPU_THREADS` environmental variable is used for OpenMM to assign"
" the number of threads per job on the CPU. If this isn't set OpenMM will use"
" all of your available CPU cores. In our case where our system only has one "
"atom, it is the most efficient to run with only one thread per walker."
msgstr ""
"`OPENMM_CPU_THREADS` は Job ごとの CPU Thread 数です。未設定では全 Core "
"を使います。1原子のこの系では、Walker ごとに1 Thread が最も効率的です。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:343
msgid ""
"This for loop iterates through every walker directory and runs `python3 "
"../../simulation_files/run.py` to begin the metadynamics simulation, and "
"submits the job as a background process with `&`. The script saves the "
"process ID and outputs it to the screen afterwards to make it easy to kill "
"the background processes if something goes wrong. On UNIX-based operating "
"systems you can run either the `top` or `htop` command to monitor the "
"background processes."
msgstr ""
"For Loop が各 Walker に移り、`python3 ../../simulation_files/run.py` を `&` で "
"Background 実行します。問題時に終了しやすいよう Process ID を保存・表示します。UNIX 系では `top`、`htop` "
"で監視できます。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:345
msgid "Beginning the simulation"
msgstr "開始"

#: markdown/inputs.md:347
msgid ""
"To begin your simulations for a given radius run the command `bash run.sh` "
"from the `data/radius_0.x` directory. If you do not modify the `run.py` "
"file, each walker will run for 100 ns to give a combined time of 400 ns. "
"This amount of time is enough for the PMFs to adequately converge. Feel free"
" to run for longer to get an even smoother profile! Once your simulations "
"have finished running, it is time to [analyse](analysis.md)."
msgstr ""
"各半径の `data/radius_0.x` で `bash run.sh` を実行します。`run.py` が既定なら各 Walker が100 "
"ns、計400 ns で、PMF の収束には十分です。さらに滑らかにしたければ長くできます。終了後は [解析](analysis.md) します。"

#: markdown/inputs.md:351
msgid "[Back to binding tutorial main page.](../NAVIGATION.md)"
msgstr "[Binding チュートリアルのメインページに戻る。](../NAVIGATION.md)"
